+# Cache Eviction Policy
+
+The project's current recorded decision is to use LRU (Least Recently Used) eviction combined with a 300-second time-to-live (TTL): entries are evicted based on recency of access, and any entry is automatically expired after 300 seconds regardless of access pattern. This combination was adopted for its simpler implementation and automatic cleanup of stale entries, and it supersedes the project's earlier decision.
